Explanation
Graph Coloring means assigning colors to vertices such that no two adjacent vertices have the same color.

Backtracking


It tries all possible color combinations.


If a color assignment is not valid, it backtracks and tries another.


Guarantees solution but is slower.



Branch and Bound


It improves backtracking by pruning invalid branches early.


Avoids unnecessary computations.


Faster than basic backtracking.



Functions Used


is_safe() → checks if color assignment is valid


graph_coloring_bt() → Backtracking solution


graph_coloring_bb() → Branch & Bound solution



Output


Displays vertex-wise color assignment


Shows step-by-step execution


Optional GUI visualization using Tkinter



Conclusion
Backtracking finds the solution by trial, while Branch & Bound optimizes it by reducing extra work.

